.TH MARBOR 1 "2026-08-17" "marbor dev" "Marbor Manual"
.SH NAME
marbor \- CLI client for the Marbor Admin API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marbor
.I command
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Marbor is a single static binary that is three tools in one - the marbor server, a marbor agent, and this thin CLI client of the Admin API - selected by the first argument. As a CLI, every subcommand below is exactly one Admin API request; it never talks to a marbor agent directly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
print CLI and (if reachable) server version
.TP
.B status
print marbor health/status summary
.TP
.B login
authenticate once and save the session locally (recommended)
.TP
.B logout
remove the saved session
.TP
.B whoami
show the CLI's saved identity (live\-verified)
.TP
.B nodes
list nodes known to marbor. See \fBmarbor-nodes\fR(1).
.TP
.B models
fleet\-wide list, or pull/delete/unload/list on one node. See \fBmarbor-models\fR(1).
.TP
.B runtime
start/stop/restart/logs/drain/undrain/health on one node. See \fBmarbor-runtime\fR(1).
.TP
.B node
node control driver operations. See \fBmarbor-node\fR(1).
.TP
.B key
per\-API-key local/cloud routing overrides (masked list, plaintext\-once on create). See \fBmarbor-key\fR(1).
.TP
.B schedules
manage time\-of-day warmup/unload/drain/undrain automations (P\-A2-03). See \fBmarbor-schedules\fR(1).
.TP
.B routing
manage routing rules and global routing strategy (P\-A2-04). See \fBmarbor-routing\fR(1).
.TP
.B cloud
manage cloud overflow providers and view budget status (P\-A2-05). See \fBmarbor-cloud\fR(1).
.TP
.B favorites
manage your starred model list (P\-A2-06a). See \fBmarbor-favorites\fR(1).
.TP
.B spill
show per\-key, per\-provider local\-vs-cloud request counts
.TP
.B activity
show unified fleet activity feed (drain, agent, runtime, node, warmup, schedule, predictive, config)
.TP
.B requests
inspect routing decisions for past requests. See \fBmarbor-requests\fR(1).
.TP
.B audit
inspect the persisted, filterable request audit log (P\-A2-08a)
.TP
.B users
manage dashboard users. See \fBmarbor-users\fR(1).
.TP
.B completion <shell>
generate a shell completion script (bash, zsh, or fish)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User error (bad arguments, unknown command, validation failure).
.TP
.B 2
Server error (the Admin API is unreachable or returned an unexpected error).
.TP
.B 3
Reserved for future partial-success reporting (batch operations); unused today.
.TP
.B 4
Authentication error (missing, invalid, or expired credentials).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MARBOR_SERVER
Admin API base URL, used when \-\-server is not given.
.TP
.B MARBOR_USERNAME
Admin username, used when \-\-username is not given.
.TP
.B MARBOR_PASSWORD
Admin password, used when \-\-password is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/marbor/session
The session saved by "marbor login" (mode 0600), under the OS user config dir - e.g. ~/.config/marbor/session on Linux, ~/Library/Application Support/marbor/session on macOS, %AppData%\emarbor\esession on Windows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
source <(marbor completion bash)
.fi
.PP
.nf
marbor completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_marbor"
.fi
.PP
.nf
marbor completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/marbor.fish
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmarbor-nodes\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-models\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-runtime\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-node\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-key\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-schedules\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-routing\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-cloud\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-favorites\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-requests\fR(1),
\fBmarbor-users\fR(1)
